**Corollary 25.3 (actual-image recovery and its promise boundary).** On the promised domain, $\mathcal B,G_{4d+13}$, raw chronology, the augmented record (SC.3) and the parser-labelled incidence/precedence expression of Definition 7.3 determine one another on their actual images. They determine the fixed-prior original future law. If retry length alone is promised to be at most $M$, a sufficient cutoff is $4\lfloor(M+1)/2\rfloor+13$, independently of all return counts and total raw length. Conversely, any sequence of actual compatible-history collisions whose first separating degrees tend to infinity must have unbounded retry alternation across the pairs.

This injectivity is promised-domain identification: both competing histories must satisfy the promise. It does not certify that a history satisfying it is uniquely identified among unrestricted competing histories by the same cutoff, nor supply a method to verify $D(u)$ from a smaller erased record.

